# Migrate the jscodeshift library to Rust

Migrate the complete first-party jscodeshift library from JavaScript to Rust 
while preserving all externally observable behavior. The migration includes the 
CLI, argument handling, file discovery, ignore rules, runner, workers, core API,
collections, node matching, templates, parser adapters, and package utilities. 
Preserve the package-root export, direct jscodeshift helpers, and existing 
JavaScript transforms including collection traversal, builders, comments, 
formatting, and supported JavaScript, TypeScript, and TSX syntax. JavaScript may
remain only as the minimal compatibility bridge required to execute those 
transforms. Use the given codebase as the migration baseline.

The public CLI, transform API, outputs, errors, options, file-writing behavior, 
and compatibility semantics must remain unchanged.

Include `app-setup/manifest.json` in the completed workspace. It is the harness 
lifecycle handoff
for this CLI task: define non-empty argument arrays under `commands` for 
`build`, `reset`, and
`start`. If JavaScript bridge modules beyond the public package entrypoints are 
retained to load
and execute transforms, list their package-relative paths in `javascriptBridge`.

```json
{
  "contractVersion": "1.0",
  "commands": {
    "build": ["bash", "app-setup/build.sh"],
    "reset": ["bash", "app-setup/reset.sh"],
    "start": ["bash", "app-setup/start.sh"]
  },
  "javascriptBridge": ["bridge/transform-host.js"]
}
```


